; THE ASHFALL HOMESTEAD (the 2026-08-28 layout rebuild) — the player's holding, east of the Embermarket.
;
; ⚠️ WHAT THIS REPLACED. A rectangle: 41 fence posts around x -19.2..15 / z -12.4..16, a gate in the
; middle of the west wall, a straight nine-stone path from that gate to a cottage at the plot's
; centre, and the three crafting stations in a column at x = 7.5 standing in open ground beside it.
; Symmetrical, centred, and readable in one glance from outside the fence.
;
; THE LAYOUT NOW — a hexagon with two clipped corners:
;   boundary        north z = -14 (x -7..16), east x = 16 (z -14..2), a SOUTH-EAST CLIP from (16, 4)
;                   to (9, 11), south z = 12 (x 8..-18), west x = -18 (z 12..-6), and a NORTH-WEST
;                   CLIP from (-18, -6) to (-8, -14).
;   the gate        a 3.9 m gap in the north-west clip at about (-12.7, -9.8), with the lamp and the
;                   deed post beside it. You enter at a corner and the plot opens diagonally.
;   the drive       curves south-east from the gate to the cottage's SOUTH door at (7, -1.5). The
;                   cottage does not rotate — its interior is authored in cell coordinates — so the
;                   door still faces +z and the path had to come round to meet it.
;   the cottage     x 6..12, z -8..-1, in the plot's NORTH-EAST corner. Interior re-planned with the
;                   hearth on the east wall, the bed in the north-west corner and the table centred.
;   the workshop    x 14, z -11..-2: forge, workbench and alchemy bench in a lean-to ROW against the
;                   east boundary, with the timber, rope and crates at its north end.
;   the kitchen     x -18..-7, z 3..12, behind a low internal fence at z = 3: the well, bushes and
;   garden          the one tree on that side.
;   THE BUILD YARD  the south lawn, local (0, 5), 7 m radius — see EmberCrownCottage.tres, whose
;                   PlacementCenter moved with this rebuild from world (58, 0, 54) to (52, 0, 51).
;                   Nothing may be authored inside that circle.
;   Veyra's shrine  (12, 4), tucked inside the south-east clip where the boundary turns.
;
; ⚠️ EVERYTHING STATIC PARENTS TO Nav. The deed post, the chest, the two weapon stands and the bed
; deliberately do not — they are interactables, and a body inside the NavigationRegion3D is a hole in
; the navmesh where a person is standing.

; ⚠️ THE NAV VOXEL GRID COARSENED WITH THE WORLD (the 2026-08-29 geography overhaul). Cells
; went from 52 m squares on a flat slab to 90-200 m of real terrain, and a 0.25 m voxel over
; five times the area is twenty-five times the columns to rasterise — the traversal probe timed
; out waiting for the bake. ⚠️ AND THE agent_* DIMS DID NOT FOLLOW. On the 0.25 grid 1.75 and
; 0.5 were whole voxels; on this one they are not, so every bake quantised them and warned. The
; values below are the QUANTISED ones, so the file now says what the bake does: agent_height and
; agent_radius CEIL to a voxel (cell_height / cell_size), agent_max_climb FLOORS to cell_height.
; ⚠️ They encode this grid — change cell_size or cell_height and recompute all three with it.
;
; ⚠️ THIS CELL AUTHORED NONE OF IT UNTIL 2026-08-31 and the header above still claimed it did. It
; baked on the NavigationMesh DEFAULTS — a 0.25 m grid over 90x90 m, which is the cost this comment
; exists to avoid, and a 1.5 m agent, which is shorter than anyone who walks here: routes were baked
; under overhangs a 1.8 m body does not fit through. It now carries the same settlement grid as every
; other 90x90 cell. The doorway takes it: the kit's door module is 2.00 m wide with NO collider
; across it and the walls are 3.12 m tall, so 1.8 m of headroom and a 0.6 m radius both clear.
[sub_resource type="NavigationMesh" id="NavMesh_home"]
vertices = PackedVector3Array()
geometry_parsed_geometry_type = 1
cell_size = 0.3
cell_height = 0.3
agent_height = 1.8
agent_radius = 0.6
agent_max_climb = 0.3
agent_max_slope = 42.0

